solnix: tzmon -- a per-zone kstat (temperature, trip points, over-limit count, the ThinkPad EC sensors), so the
live media can print a temperature line without dtrace.

WHY
- The installer media's console temperature line (solnix-diag's temp service) needs the zone's _TMP. The tz__temp
  SDT probe is unusable there: dtrace cannot load its CTF on the media (the libz / LIBCTF_DECOMPRESSOR gap).
- A kstat is the illumos interface for a driver's live counters. kstat(1M) reads it, and an unread kstat costs
  nothing.

THE CHANGE (applies on top of 0002-tzmon-thinkpad-hkey-enable.patch)
- kstat tzmon:<instance>:<zone>, <zone> being the zone's ACPI name (THM0), class misc, named:
    temp_C     the last _TMP the monitor polled (no ACPI evaluation when the kstat is read);
    hot_C, crt_C   the trip points (-1 = none);
    overlimit  the consecutive over-limit count (0002's debounce);
    ec_gput    the ThinkPad EC's GPUT byte (dGPU temperature, C), -1 elsewhere;
    ec_tmp0-7  the EC's TMP0-7 (C), -1 where the EC has no such field.
  The EC fields are read in ks_update, i.e. only when someone reads the kstat. ks_lock is the zone lock, so a read
  never races the monitor. The kstat is deleted before the zone is freed.
- tzmon_report() and the kstat share one EC reader (tzmon_ec_temps).
- X1 Extreme Gen5, BIOS N3JET48W (dsdt.dsl in solnix-bank/evidence/x1e-acpi-N3JET48W): the EC names TMP0 at 0x78,
  then GPUT, TTS1-TTS4 at 0x79-0x7E (lines 27633-27640), and TSL0-3 at 0x88-0x8B (lines 27650-27657). THM0._TMP
  (lines 67457-67490) reads TMP0, TSL2 and TSL3, maps a 0x80 TMP0 to 0x30 (48 C), and returns TCRT only when TSL3 is
  set, or TSL2 while HKEY.DHKC is 0. TC2K clamps out-of-range values to 48 C. That is the same logic as the P1 Gen4
  sibling that 0002's header describes. TMP1-7 therefore read -1 on the X1E, and ec_gput carries the dGPU reading.
